    "text": "Lucas se godspellere, \u00fee w\u00e6s l\u00e6ce on life, and he manega geh\u00e6lde fram mislicum co\u00f0um mid his\nNe fordeme ge, and ge ne beo\u00f0 fordemede; forgifa\u00f0 o\u00f0rum mannum, and eow bi\u00f0 forgifen.\nD\u00e6la\u00f0 and do\u00f0 god, and eow bi\u00f0 god forgifen.\nHy forgifa\u00f0 eft into eowrum bosme swi\u00f0e god gemet \u00feam \u00fee ge nu d\u00e6la\u00f0, and gecrammod gemet, and\nOn \u00f0am gemete \u00fee ge ameta\u00f0 eow bi\u00f0 eft ameten.\nHe s\u00e6de eac so\u00f0lice hym \u00feis bigspell \u00feus: Hu m\u00e6g la se blinda l\u00e6dan \u00feone blindan, and hu ne fealla\u00f0\nNe bi\u00f0 na se leorningcniht fur\u00f0or \u00feonne his lareow; \u00e6lc \u00fe\u00e6ra bi\u00f0 fulfremed \u00fee bi\u00f0 swa swa his lareow.\nHu miht \u00feu la geseon \u00fe\u00e6t mot to gewissan on \u00f0ines bro\u00f0or eagan, and \u00feone beam ne gesihst \u00fee is\nAc ateoh, \u00feu hiwere, \u00e6rest \u00feone beam ut of \u00f0inum eagan, and \u00feu locast \u00feonne \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feu of \u00f0ines bro\u00feor\nHer syndon syllice word saml\u00e6redum mannum; nu wylle we eow geopenian \u00fe\u00e6t andgit \u00fe\u00e6rto, and eow\nSe H\u00e6lend us bebead on \u00feisum halgan godspelle, Beo\u00f0 mildheorte eornostlice, eal swa eower F\u00e6der is.\nHer ge magon gehyran \u00fe\u00e6s H\u00e6lendes godnysse, \u00feonne he cw\u00e6\u00f0 swa be us, \u00fe\u00e6t we swylcne F\u00e6der us\nSe hata\u00f0 his Scyppend, se \u00f0e forsih\u00f0 his h\u00e6se, and nele mid weorcum his word gefyllan, ac swa\u00f0eah\nHe het us beon mildheorte o\u00f0rum mannum symble, mid ealre godnysse, swa swa God sylf is; ac se ne\nNe sceolde he n\u00e6fre softnysse brucan, se \u00f0e ne m\u00e6g ge\u00feafian his under\u00feeoddum mannum \u00fe\u00e6t hy lisse\nGod lufa\u00f0 \u00fea li\u00f0nysse, \u00fe\u00e6t man lissige o\u00f0rum on hefegum geswincum \u00fee men habba\u00f0 on gewunan, on\nBe Godes mildheortnysse cw\u00e6\u00f0 se witega \u00feus: Misericordiam et iudicium cantabo tibi, Domine: Ic\nSwi\u00f0e mildheort he is \u00feam \u00fee hihta\u00f0 on hine, ac swi\u00f0est \u00feam welwillendum, and \u00feam rihtge\u00f0ancedum,\n\u00de\u00e6t godspell s\u00e6ge\u00f0 gyt for\u00f0 \u00feus be endebyrdnysse: Ne deme ge nateshwon, and ge ne beo\u00f0 gedemede.\nNe forbead he mid ealle \u00e6lcne dom \u00feam witan, \u00feam \u00fee deman sceal, ac \u00f0a dyrstignysse, \u00fe\u00e6t man\nSume \u00feing synd nu digle, \u00fee God sylf deme\u00fe eft, and sume \u00feing synd opene, be \u00f0am man deman sceal,\nIacob se rihtwisa awrat on his pistole, \u00feam men bi\u00f0 dom geset butan mildheortnysse eft, se \u00f0e nu\nForgifa\u00f0 o\u00f0rum mannum, and eow bi\u00f0 forgifen.\nGod hat us forgifan ure teonan mannum, \u00fe\u00e6t he us forgife ure synna \u00feurh \u00fe\u00e6t.\nD\u00e6la\u00f0 and do\u00f0 god, and eow bi\u00f0 god forgifen.\nSe \u00f0e d\u00e6le\u00f0 for Gode, God geeacna\u00f0 his \u00feing, and him eft be hundfealdum his \u00e6lmessan forgylt.\nHy forgyfa\u00f0 eft into eowrum bosme swi\u00f0e god gemet, \u00feam \u00fee ge nu d\u00e6la\u00f0, and gecrammod gemet,\nHe m\u00e6nde \u00fea \u00feearfan, \u00fee man nu de\u00f0 god, \u00fe\u00e6t hy sceolon ageldan us eft \u00fe\u00e6t gemet; ac God sylf agylt\nOn \u00f0am gemete \u00fee ge ameta\u00f0 eow bi\u00f0 eft ameten.\n\u00deis m\u00e6g beon gecweden be eallum urum d\u00e6dum, ge worda ge weorca, \u00fe\u00e6t God witodlice \u00e6lcum men\nHe s\u00e6de eac so\u00felice hym \u00feis bigspell \u00feus: Hu m\u00e6g la se blinda l\u00e6dan \u00feone blindan, and hu ne fealla\u00f0\nBispell getacna\u00f0 on bocum gelome o\u00f0er \u00feing on wordum and o\u00f0er on getacnungum.\nNu ne m\u00e6g nan lareow, butan he \u00f0a lare h\u00e6bbe, \u00fea l\u00e6wedan men gerihtl\u00e6can to Godes rihtwisnysse,\nNe bi\u00f0 na se leorningcniht fur\u00f0or \u00feonne his lareow; \u00e6lc \u00fe\u00e6ra bi\u00f0 fulfremed \u00fee bi\u00f0 swa swa his lareaw.\nCrist sylf is se lareaw, and he sealde us bysne, \u00fe\u00e6t we sceolan mildsian, swa swa he mildsa\u00f0 us; and\nM\u00e6nig leorningcild leornode foroft \u00fe\u00e6t he mare cu\u00f0e on micclum andgyte \u00feonne his agen lareow, \u00fee\nHu miht \u00feu la geseon \u00fe\u00e6t mot to gewissan on \u00feines bro\u00f0or eagan, and \u00f0one beam ne gesihst \u00fee is\nNe m\u00e6g se langa beam licgan on \u00feinum eagan, ac se beam getacna\u00f0 \u00fea teonfullan hatunge, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feu\nBe \u00f0am ylcan andgyte he cw\u00e6\u00f0 on o\u00f0re stowe, Liquantes culicem et glutientes camelum: Hy\n\u00de\u00e6t is, \u00fe\u00e6t hy t\u00e6la\u00f0 mid teonfullum mode and mid modignysse, \u00fee is gylta m\u00e6st, \u00fea lytlan gyltas,\nAc ateoh, \u00feu hywere, \u00e6rest \u00feone beam ut of \u00feinum eagan, and \u00f0u locast \u00feonne \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feu of \u00f0ines bro\u00f0or\nHiwere bi\u00f0 se mann \u00fee hoga\u00f0 ymbe \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6t he o\u00f0erne gerihtl\u00e6ce \u00e6r hine sylfne, swylce he leahtras\n\u00dea men sceolon styran \u00fee to styrene agon, \u00fe\u00e6t syndon \u00fea witan, \u00fee \u00f0one wisdom habba\u00f0 and fram\nWe willa\u00f0 eow secgan sume bysne be \u00f0ysum, hu se H\u00e6lend sylf her on life dyde: He becom to \u00f0am\n\u00deis hy s\u00e6don to him \u00fe\u00e6t hy his fandodon, \u00fe\u00e6t hy mihton wyrcan sume wrohte be him, gif he \u00feurh his\nHe \u00f0a beah adun, and awrat mid his fingre swa on \u00f0\u00e6re eor\u00f0an, and hy acsodon \u00fea gyt.\n\u00dea s\u00e6t se H\u00e6lend upp and s\u00e6de hym \u00feus to: Swa hwylc eower swa n\u00e6f\u00f0 nane synne on him, awyrpe\nHw\u00e6t \u00fea, \u00f0a heafodmen, \u00fea hy \u00feis gehyrdon, eodon hym ealle ut endemes hire fram, and \u00fe\u00e6t wif stod\nHe s\u00e6t \u00fea eft up and s\u00e6de to \u00f0am wife, Hw\u00e6r syndon nu, la wif, \u00fea \u00fee \u00f0e wregdon swa swi\u00f0e; ne\n\u00de\u00e6t wif him andwyrde, mid afyrhtum mode, Na, leofa Drihten, ne fordemde heora nan me.\nSe H\u00e6lend hire cw\u00e6\u00f0 to, Ne ic \u00f0e ne fordeme; gang \u00feu nu aweg, and \u00feu heonan for\u00f0 ne synga.\nOn \u00f0a wisan he forgeaf \u00feone gylt \u00feam wife, \u00fe\u00e6t heo sy\u00f0\u00f0an sceolde wi\u00f0 swylc \u00feing hy gehealdan, for\nGewissige us se H\u00e6lend to his willan \u00e6fre, \u00feam is wuldor and lof a to weorulde, AMEN.",
